tions. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Secondo il testo, qual è il problema delle allusioni?","options":["Che è facile non accorgersene","Che sono maleducate","Che richiedono molto tempo","Che offendono sempre"]},"answer":"Che è facile non accorgersene","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il testo dice: “The problem is that hints are easy to miss”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u01-l04-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u01-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Un post di un blog su come dare un parere difficile.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Che differenza fa il testo tra straightforward e blunt?","options":["Si può essere chiari senza essere bruschi","Sono la stessa cosa","Essere bruschi funziona meglio","Bisogna evitare di essere chiari"]},"answer":"Si può essere chiari senza essere bruschi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il testo dice: “Being straightforward does not mean being blunt”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u01-l04-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u01-l04","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u1-feedback-post","document":"post","setting":"Un post di un blog su come dare un parere difficile.","title":"How to say difficult things","lines":["Most of us tend to avoid difficult conversations. We are afraid of hurting people, so we say nothing, or we drop a hint and hope the other person understands.","The problem is that hints are easy to miss. Your colleague may not realize there is a problem at all.","Being straightforward does not mean being blunt. Start with something positive, then point out the problem clearly and calmly, and finally look for a solution together.","Remember: people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm."]},"question":"Secondo il testo, che cosa accettano peggio le persone?","options":["Il sarcasmo","Un parere sincero","Un commento positivo","Una soluzione trovata insieme"]},"answer":"Il sarcasmo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il testo dice: “people can accept honest feedback when it is tactful. What they find hard to accept is sarcasm”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u01-l04-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u01-l04","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","options":["Don't bring up politics at dinner.","Don't bring up politics at work.","Do bring up politics at dinner.","Don't talk about politics at dinner."]},"answer":"Don't bring up politics at dinner.","accep