_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"You can borrow my car ___ you drive carefully.","translation":"Puoi usare la mia macchina, purché tu guidi con prudenza.","options":["as long as","in case","otherwise","although"]},"answer":"as long as","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"As long as + presente: la condizione perché qualcosa succeda.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-as-long-as"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Take an umbrella ___ it rains.","translation":"Porta un ombrello, nel caso piova.","options":["in case","as long as","otherwise","unless"]},"answer":"in case","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In case: fai qualcosa prima, per precauzione.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-in-case"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Hurry up. ___, we will miss the train.","translation":"Sbrigati. Altrimenti perderemo il treno.","options":["Otherwise","Provided that","In case","As long as"]},"answer":"Otherwise","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-otherwise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We will sign, provided that the price ___ the same.","translation":"Firmeremo, a condizione che il prezzo resti lo stesso.","options":["stays","will stay","stayed","would stay"]},"answer":"stays","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dopo provided that (come dopo if) va il presente, anche se parli del futuro e anche se in italiano useresti il congiuntivo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-provided-that"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Una candidata risponde a un’offerta di lavoro.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"Che condizione pone Laura per accettare l’offerta?","options":["Continuare a lavorare da casa due giorni alla settimana","Uno stipendio più alto","Cominciare il mese prossimo","Avere un suo team"]},"answer":"Continuare a lavorare da casa due giorni alla settimana","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura scrive: “I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-offer","document":"email","setting":"Una candidata risponde a un’offerta di lavoro.","from":"Laura Kim","to":"Mr. Patel","title":"Job offer","lines":["Dear Mr. Patel,","Thank you very much for the job offer. I am very excited about joining the team.","Before I accept, I would like to discuss one point. In my current job I work from home two days a week, and this flexibility is important to me.","I would be happy to accept a slightly lower salary, provided that I can keep those two days at home. Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down.","I hope we can reach an agreement. I am free to talk at any time this week.","Kind regards,","Laura Kim"]},"question":"Che cosa succede se l’azienda non accetta la sua condizione?","options":["Laura rifiuterà l’offerta","Laura accetterà lo stesso","Laura chiederà più tempo","Laura parlerà con il suo capo attuale"]},"answer":"Laura rifiuterà l’offerta","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Laura scrive: “Otherwise, I am afraid I would have to turn the offer down”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","options":["Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","Send me the terms in writing, as long as nothing changes.","Send me the terms by email, in case anything changes.","Send them the terms in writing, in case anything changes."]},"answer":"Send me the terms in writing, in case anything changes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-in-case"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["I","will","help","you","as","long","as","you","help","me"],"translation":"Ti aiuterò, purché tu aiuti me."},"answer":"I will help you as long as you help me.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-as-long-as"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you taking a jacket? (nel caso faccia freddo)","translation":"Perché ti porti una giacca?"},"answer":"In case it gets cold.","accepted_answers":["In case it's cold.","I am taking it in case it gets cold.","I'm taking a jacket in case it gets cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-in-case"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l03-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Sbrigati. Altrimenti perderemo il treno."},"answer":"Hurry up. Otherwise, we will miss the train.","accepted_answers":["Hurry up. Otherwise, we'll miss the train.","Hurry up. Otherwise we will miss the train.","Hurry up, otherwise we'll miss the train."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-otherwise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"leader","right":"leader / capo"},{"left":"delegate","right":"delegare"},{"left":"workload","right":"carico di lavoro"},{"left":"persuade","right":"convincere / persuadere"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-leader","eit-delegate","eit-workload","eit-persuade"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"She took ___ a new project last week.","translation":"La settimana scorsa si è presa un nuovo progetto.","options":["on","up","off","down"]},"answer":"on","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-take-on"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I persuaded my boss ___ me a day off.","translation":"Ho convinto il mio capo a darmi un giorno libero.","options":["to give","giving","give","gave"]},"answer":"to give","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Persuade someone to + verbo (come «convincere qualcuno a»).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-persuade"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Una team leader parla con un dipendente sommerso di lavoro.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Perché Omar ha così tanto lavoro?","options":["Si è preso un cliente nuovo e continua a seguire i progetti di prima","Un collega si è licenziato","Sta imparando un lavoro nuovo","La sua capa gli ha dato le relazioni di Ben"]},"answer":"Si è preso un cliente nuovo e continua a seguire i progetti di prima","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Omar dice: “I took on the new client last month, and I’m still doing my old projects”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-team","setting":"Una team leader parla con un dipendente sommerso di lavoro.","speakers":[{"name":"Grace","voice":"a"},{"name":"Omar","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Grace","text":"Omar, you look exhausted. Is your workload too heavy at the moment?"},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Honestly, yes. I took on the new client last month, and I'm still doing my old projects."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"You should have told me. A good leader needs to know these things."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"I didn't want to turn down the client. I thought it was a good opportunity."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"It is, but you can't do everything. Let's delegate the reports to Ben."},{"speaker":"Omar","text":"Are you sure? He is quite new."},{"speaker":"Grace","text":"That's fine. I'll help him at the beginning, in case he has questions."}]},"question":"Che soluzione propone Grace?","options":["Delegare le relazioni a Ben e aiutarlo all’inizio","Rifiutare il cliente nuovo","Assumere un’altra persona","Che Omar lavori nel fine settimana"]},"answer":"Delegare le relazioni a Ben e aiutarlo all’inizio","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Grace dice: “Let’s delegate the reports to Ben… I’ll help him at the beginning”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo di una rivista sulla leadership.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"Secondo l’articolo, perché conviene convincere invece di dare ordini?","options":["Perché un team che capisce il motivo lavora di più perché la decisione funzioni","Perché gli ordini sono illegali","Perché così il leader lavora meno","Perché il team ha sempre ragione"]},"answer":"Perché un team che capisce il motivo lavora di più perché la decisione funzioni","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"A good leader listens to the team.","options":["A good leader listens to the team.","A good leader talks to the team.","A good leader listens to the client.","The good leaders listen to the team."]},"answer":"A good leader listens to the team.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-leader"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":8,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u2-leader","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo di una rivista sulla leadership.","title":"Leaders, not bosses","lines":["What makes a good leader? Many people imagine someone who gives orders and never changes their mind. Research shows the opposite.","The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise when a better idea appears.","They also know how to delegate. Instead of doing everything themselves, they give people responsibility and trust them to do the job.","Finally, they persuade rather than order. When a team understands the reason for a decision, it works harder to make it succeed."]},"question":"Secondo l’articolo, come sono i leader migliori?","options":["Flessibili: ascoltano e cedono se arriva un’idea migliore","Fermi: non cambiano mai idea","Esigenti: danno ordini chiari","Indipendenti: fanno tutto da soli"]},"answer":"Flessibili: ascoltano e cedono se arriva un’idea migliore","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “The best leaders are flexible. They listen first, and they are willing to compromise”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How is work at the moment? (hai troppo lavoro)","translation":"Come va il lavoro in questo periodo?"},"answer":"My workload is too heavy.","accepted_answers":["My workload is too heavy at the moment.","I have too much work.","My workload is very heavy."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-workload"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u02-l04-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u02-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"La settimana scorsa si è presa un nuovo progetto."},"answer":"She took on a new project last week.","accepted_answers":["Last week she took on a new project.","He took on a new project last week.","Last week he took on a new project."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-take-on"]},{"id":"eit-b2-