ta la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Working from home is a growing ___.","translation":"Lavorare da casa è una tendenza in crescita.","options":["trend","custom","society","generation"]},"answer":"trend","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-trend"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In some countries it is a ___ to take off your shoes at home.","translation":"In alcuni paesi è usanza togliersi le scarpe in casa.","options":["custom","trend","society","habit"]},"answer":"custom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Custom: usanza di una società. Habit: abitudine di una persona.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-custom"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast intervista una sociologa sulle generazioni.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Secondo la sociologa, che cosa dice ogni generazione di quella successiva?","options":["Che non rispetta le usanze di una volta","Che lavora di più","Che vive meglio","Che è più felice"]},"answer":"Che non rispetta le usanze di una volta","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il conduttore chiede se i giovani non rispettano le usanze e lei risponde: “Every generation has said that about the next one”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast intervista una sociologa sulle generazioni.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Che cosa è cambiato e che cosa no, secondo la sociologa?","options":["Sono cambiate le usanze, ma non i valori","Sono cambiati i valori, ma non le usanze","Non è cambiato niente","È cambiato tutto"]},"answer":"Sono cambiate le usanze, ma non i valori","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: “Customs change, of course… But the values behind them haven’t disappeared”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Technology has changed our society.","options":["Technology has changed our society.","Technology will change our society.","Technology has changed our generation.","The internet has changed our society."]},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-society"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","generation","grew","up","with","the","internet"],"translation":"La mia generazione è cresciuta con internet."},"answer":"My generation grew up with the internet.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-generation"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What is a big trend in your country? (lavorare da casa)","translation":"Qual è una grande tendenza nel tuo paese?"},"answer":"Working from home is a big trend.","accepted_answers":["Working from home.","Working from home is a growing trend.","Working from home is a trend."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-trend"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l01-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"La tecnologia ha cambiato la nostra società."},"answer":"Technology has changed our society.","accepted_answers":["Technology changed our society.","Technology's changed our society."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-society"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"population","right":"popolazione"},{"left":"majority","right":"maggioranza"},{"left":"minority","right":"minoranza"},{"left":"survey","right":"sondaggio / indagine"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-population","eit-majority","eit-minority","eit-survey"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Prices have ___ a lot this year.","translation":"I prezzi sono aumentati molto quest’anno.","options":["risen","rose","rise","rised"]},"answer":"risen","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Rise è irregolare: rise, rose, risen. Con have va il participio: have risen.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-rise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The ___ family has fewer than two children.","translation":"La famiglia media ha meno di due figli.","options":["average","majority","minority","population"]},"answer":"average","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-average"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo su un sondaggio sulle persone che vivono da sole.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"Com’è cambiato il numero delle famiglie di una sola persona?","options":["È passato da una su dieci a una su quattro","È passato da una su quattro a una su dieci","Non è cambiato","Si è dimezzato"]},"answer":"È passato da una su dieci a una su quattro","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo su un sondaggio sulle persone che vivono da sole.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"Che cosa dice il sondaggio sull’idea che vivere da soli faccia sentire soli?","options":["Che la maggior parte di chi vive da solo dice di essere felice","Che è vera","Che vale solo per i giovani","Che non l’ha chiesto"]},"answer":"Che la maggior parte di chi vive da solo dice di essere felice","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-alone","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo su un sondaggio sulle persone che vivono da sole.","title":"A table for one","lines":["Living alone used to be unusual. Today it is one of the biggest trends in our society.","According to a recent survey, one in four homes now has only one person in it. Fifty years ago, the figure was one in ten.","The majority of people who live alone are over sixty, but the number of young people living alone is also rising.","It is often said that living alone makes people lonely. However, the survey suggests the opposite: most people who live alone said they were happy with their lives.","What has declined is the number of large families. In 1970 the average family had four children. Today it has fewer than two."]},"question":"Che cosa è diminuito, secondo l’articolo?","options":["Il numero delle famiglie numerose","Il numero degli anziani","Il numero delle abitazioni","Il numero dei giovani"]},"answer":"Il numero delle famiglie numerose","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “What has declined is the number of large families”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The population of the city has risen.","options":["The population of the city has risen.","The population of the city has declined.","The population of the country has risen.","The population of the city will rise."]},"answer":"The population of the city has risen.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-population","eit-rise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Only","a","minority","of","students","live","alone"],"translation":"Solo una minoranza degli studenti vive da sola."},"answer":"Only a minority of students live alone.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-minority"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Has the number of large families risen? (no, è diminuito)","translation":"Il numero delle famiglie numerose è aumentato?"},"answer":"No, it has declined.","accepted_answers":["No, it's declined.","No, it declined.","No. It has declined."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-decline"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l02-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l02","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Secondo un sondaggio, la maggior parte delle persone è felice."},"answer":"According to a survey, the majority of people are happy.","accepted_answers":["According to a survey, most people are happy.","According to a survey the majority of people are happy.","According to a survey, the majority of people is happy."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-survey","eit-majority"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":1,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["My","generation","grew","up","with","the","internet"],"translation":"La mia generazione è cresciuta con internet."},"answer":"My generation grew up with the internet.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-generation"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":2,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"aumentare / salire"},"answer":"rise","accepted_answers":["risen","rose"],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-rise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":3,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Scrivi la parola completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"p_p_l_t_o_","hint":"popolazione"},"answer":"population","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["eit-population"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In some countries it is a ___ to take off your shoes at home.","translation":"In alcuni paesi è usanza togliersi le scarpe in casa.","options":["custom","trend","society","habit"]},"answer":"custom","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Custom: usanza di una società. Habit: abitudine di una persona.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-custom"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":5,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “average”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"average","options":["medio / nella media","sondaggio / indagine","diversità","abitudine"]},"answer":"medio / nella media","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-average"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":6,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"average","right":"medio / nella media"},{"left":"generation","right":"generazione"},{"left":"population","right":"popolazione"},{"left":"rise","right":"aumentare / salire"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-average","eit-generation","eit-population","eit-rise"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Only","a","minority","of","students","live","alone"],"translation":"Solo una minoranza degli studenti vive da sola."},"answer":"Only a minority of students live alone.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-minority"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"trend","options":["trend","it is said that","be expected to","rise"]},"answer":"trend","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-trend"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":9,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"generation","options":["generation","average","population","housing"]},"answer":"generation","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-generation"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-rev1","position":10,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Has the number of large families risen? (no, è diminuito)","translation":"Il numero delle famiglie numerose è aumentato?"},"answer":"No, it has declined.","accepted_answers":["No, it's declined.","No, it declined.","No. It has declined."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-decline"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It is ___ that the house is two hundred years old.","translation":"Si dice che la casa abbia duecento anni.","options":["said","saying","say","told"]},"answer":"said","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Passivo impersonale: It is said / believed that + frase.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-it-is-said"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The new homes are expected ___ ready next year.","translation":"Si prevede che le case nuove siano pronte l’anno prossimo.","options":["to be","being","be","will be"]},"answer":"to be","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Be expected + to + verbo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"It is a ___ idea, but it is not true.","translation":"È un’idea molto diffusa, ma non è vera.","options":["widespread","average","local","lonely"]},"answer":"widespread","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-widespread"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast intervista una sociologa sulle generazioni.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Perché la sociologa cita gli antichi greci?","options":["Per mostrare che la lamentela sui giovani è antichissima","Per parlare della storia della Grecia","Per dire che i greci erano migliori","Per spiegare un’usanza greca"]},"answer":"Per mostrare che la lamentela sui giovani è antichissima","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: “It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-podcast","setting":"Un podcast intervista una sociologa sulle generazioni.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Reyes","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"People often complain that young people have no respect for old customs. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Every generation has said that about the next one. It is said that even the ancient Greeks complained about their teenagers."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"So nothing has really changed?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Customs change, of course. Fewer people get married in church, for example, and family dinners are less common. But the values behind them haven't disappeared."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What do you mean?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Young people still care about their families. They just show it in different ways: a video call instead of a Sunday lunch."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is the gap between generations getting bigger?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Reyes","text":"Honestly, I don't think so. Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things."}]},"question":"Che cosa pensa la sociologa dell’idea che la distanza tra le generazioni sia sempre più grande?","options":["Che molti ci credono, ma la sua ricerca non lo conferma","Che è vera","Che è un’idea nuova","Che nessuno ci crede"]},"answer":"Che molti ci credono, ma la sua ricerca non lo conferma","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: “Many people believe that, but my research shows that parents and children agree about most things”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u3-market","document":"notice","setting":"Un avviso del comune sul vecchio mercato.","title":"Our market is changing","lines":["The old market is being renovated and will be closed until the end of May.","The roof has already been repaired, and new lights are being installed this month.","The market has been used by local families for more than a hundred years. It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood.","When the work is finished, the market will be used for concerts and festivals. The first festival is expected to take place in June.","Questions can be sent to the community office."]},"question":"Che cosa si crede del mercato?","options":["Che è l’edificio più antico del quartiere","Che chiuderà per sempre","Che è il più grande della città","Che l’ha costruito una famiglia"]},"answer":"Che è l’edificio più antico del quartiere","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’avviso dice: “It is believed to be the oldest building in the neighborhood”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","options":["It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said that the house is three hundred years old.","It was said that the house was two hundred years old.","They say that the house is two hundred years old."]},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-it-is-said"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["The","festival","is","expected","to","take","place","in","June"],"translation":"Si prevede che il festival si svolga a giugno."},"answer":"The festival is expected to take place in June.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-be-expected-to","eit-take-place"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"When will the homes be ready? (si prevede che siano pronte l’anno prossimo)","translation":"Quando saranno pronte le case?"},"answer":"They are expected to be ready next year.","accepted_answers":["They're expected to be ready next year.","They are expected to be finished next year.","Next year, they are expected to be ready."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-be-expected-to"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u03-l03-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u03-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Si dice che la casa abbia duecento anni."},"answer":"It is said that the house is two hundred years old.","accepted_answers":["It's said that the house is two hundred years old.","It is said the house is two hundred years old.","The house is said to be t