he next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"Che cos’ha di speciale il filtro di Mei Lin?","options":["È economico e pulisce l’acqua solo con la luce del sole","È il più grande del mondo","Funziona con l’elettricità","L’ha inventato il conduttore"]},"answer":"È economico e pulisce l’acqua solo con la luce del sole","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mei dice: “Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u04-l02-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u04-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u4-interview","setting":"Un’intervista alla radio a una scienziata che ha inventato un filtro per l’acqua.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mei","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"My guest today is Dr. Mei Lin, whose team has come up with a new way to clean water. Welcome."},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Thank you. Our filter, which costs less than five dollars, uses only sunlight to clean dirty water."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"That sounds like a real breakthrough. How did you get the idea?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"By accident, actually. One of our experiments failed, which was very frustrating at the time. But the results showed something we didn't expect."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And is there evidence that it works outside the lab?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"Yes. We have tested it in forty villages, most of which have no clean water. The data are very clear."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"What is the next step?"},{"speaker":"Mei","text":"We want to make it in large numbers. The invention is useless if the people who need it can't get it."}]},"question":"Che cosa vuole dire Mei con “The invention is useless if the people who need it can’t get it”?","options":["Che l’invenzione serve solo se arriva a chi ne ha bisogno","Che l’invenzione non funziona","Che è molto cara","Che nessuno ne ha bisogno"]},"answer":"Che l’invenzione serve solo se arriva a chi ne ha bisogno","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Per questo il prossimo passo è produrlo in grandi quantità: “We want to make it in large numbers”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u04-l02-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u04-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u4-museum","document":"notice","setting":"Cartelli di una sala di un museo della scienza.","title":"Science Museum","lines":["Room 3: Ideas that changed the world","The telephone, which was invented in 1876, allowed people to talk across long distances for the first time.","Marie Curie, whose discoveries changed medicine, was the first person to win two Nobel Prizes.","The World Wide Web was created by Tim Berners-Lee, a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment for his invention.","Which of these innovations do you use every day?"]},"question":"Che cosa si sottolinea di Tim Berners-Lee?","options":["Che per lui condividere le informazioni contava più dei soldi","Che ha inventato il telefono","Che ha vinto due premi Nobel","Che si è fatto pagare molto per la sua invenzione"]},"answer":"Che per lui condividere le informazioni contava più dei soldi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il cartello dice: “a scientist for whom sharing information was more important than money. He never asked for payment”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u04-l02-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u04-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"t