,{"speaker":"Customer","text":"Hmm. Is it worth it? The phone is three years old."},{"speaker":"Assistant","text":"Honestly, the older the phone, the less sense it makes. A new one costs about four hundred."},{"speaker":"Customer","text":"I can't afford a new one right now. Go ahead and replace the screen, please."}]},"question":"Perché questa volta lo schermo costa il doppio?","options":["Perché è originale; l’ultima volta gliene hanno messo uno più economico","Perché il telefono è nuovo","Perché lo consegnano oggi","Perché i prezzi sono aumentati"]},"answer":"Perché è originale; l’ultima volta gliene hanno messo uno più economico","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il commesso dice: “Last time you had a cheaper screen put in. This one is original. The cheaper ones are nowhere near as good”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u05-l04-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u05-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u5-savings","document":"post","setting":"Un post di un blog su come risparmiare.","title":"How I saved $3,000 in a year","lines":["Last January I looked at my bank account and realized I had no savings at all. So I decided to change a few things.","First, I cut back on subscriptions. I was paying for four streaming services and a gym I never went to. Canceling them saved me sixty dollars a month.","Second, I started buying second-hand clothes and furniture. Most of it is in perfect condition and costs half the price.","Third, before buying anything, I ask myself one question: is this good value for money, or do I just want it?","One year later, I have saved three thousand dollars. It was by far the best decision I made last year."]},"question":"Come giudica l’autrice la sua decisione di risparmiare?","options":["Come di gran lunga la decisione migliore dell’anno scorso","Come un errore","Come una cosa