","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"deludere / tradire la fiducia di qualcuno"},"answer":"let down","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-let-down"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Are you still angry with your sister? (no, avete già fatto pace)","translation":"Sei ancora arrabbiato con tua sorella?"},"answer":"No, we have made up.","accepted_answers":["No, we've made up.","No, we made up.","No. We have made up."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-make-up"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2","position":9,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Don't talk to him now. He is in a bad ___.","translation":"Non parlargli adesso. È di cattivo umore.","options":["mood","tone","day","time"]},"answer":"mood","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Be in a good / bad mood: essere di buon / cattivo umore.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-mood"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-rev2","position":10,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I fell ___ with my best friend last week.","translation":"La settimana scorsa ho litigato con la mia migliore amica.","options":["out","up","down","off"]},"answer":"out","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-fall-out"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “self-confidence”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"self-confidence","options":["fiducia in sé stessi / sicurezza","empatia","umore / stato d’animo","in colpa / colpevole"]},"answer":"fiducia in sé stessi / sicurezza","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-self-confidence"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ means understanding how others feel.","translation":"Empatia significa capire come si sentono gli altri.","options":["Empathy","Mood","Self-confidence","Diversity"]},"answer":"Empathy","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-empathy"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Learning a language gave me more ___.","translation":"Imparare una lingua mi ha dato più fiducia in me stesso.","options":["self-confidence","empathy","mood","evidence"]},"answer":"self-confidence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-self-confidence"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast di psicologia intervista uno psicologo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Secondo lo psicologo, l’empatia è la stessa cosa che essere d’accordo?","options":["No: è capire come si sente l’altro, anche se non sei d’accordo","Sì, è la stessa cosa","Sì, ma solo con gli amici","No: è dare consigli"]},"answer":"No: è capire come si sente l’altro, anche se non sei d’accordo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: “It is the ability to understand how another person feels… It’s not the same as agreeing with them”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast di psicologia intervista uno psicologo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Che cosa può esserci dietro il fatto di essere spesso di cattivo umore?","options":["Stress o mancanza di sonno","Una cattiva alimentazione","Troppo lavoro di squadra","Il tempo atmosferico"]},"answer":"Stress o mancanza di sonno","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Dice: “if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u06-l05-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u06-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u6-podcast","setting":"Un podcast di psicologia intervista uno psicologo.","speakers":[{"name":"Host","voice":"a"},{"name":"Dr. Moss","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Host","text":"Today we are talking about empathy. What exactly is it?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"It is the ability to understand how another person feels, to put yourself in their shoes. It's not the same as agreeing with them."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Can empathy be learned?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Yes. The first step is to listen without judging. Most of us listen only to answer."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"Some listeners say their mood changes very quickly. Is that normal?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"Everybody has good and bad days. But if you are often in a bad mood, it might be stress, or a lack of sleep."},{"speaker":"Host","text":"And what about self-confidence?"},{"speaker":"Dr. Moss","text":"People with low self-confidence tend to think that others are judging them. Usually, others are too busy thinking about themselves!"}]},"question":"Che co