vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Extreme weather is a ___ of global warming.","translation":"Il clima estremo è una conseguenza del riscaldamento globale.","options":["consequence","emissions","footprint","solution"]},"answer":"consequence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-consequence"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo d’opinione sull’impronta di carbonio.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"Qual è l’idea principale dell’articolo?","options":["Che i cambiamenti individuali aiutano, ma non bastano senza grandi cambiamenti","Che le docce brevi salvano il pianeta","Che non bisogna fare niente","Che le aziende non inquinano"]},"answer":"Che i cambiamenti individuali aiutano, ma non bastano senza grandi cambiamenti","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “These things matter, but they are not enough” e propone il passaggio all’energia rinnovabile.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo d’opinione sull’impronta di carbonio.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"Che cosa confronta l’autore con whereas?","options":["Quello che risparmia una famiglia con quello che produce una fabbrica","Due tipi di energia","Due paesi","La carne e il pesce"]},"answer":"Quello che risparmia una famiglia con quello che produce una fabbrica","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":6,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Global warming is changing the weather.","options":["Global warming is changing the weather.","Global warming is changing the world.","Global warming has changed the weather.","Pollution is changing the weather."]},"answer":"Global warming is changing the weather.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-global-warming"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":7,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Cars","produce","a","lot","of","emissions"],"translation":"Le auto producono molte emissioni."},"answer":"Cars produce a lot of emissions.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-emissions"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"How can you reduce your carbon footprint? (mangiare meno carne)","translation":"Come puoi ridurre la tua impronta di carbonio?"},"answer":"I can eat less meat.","accepted_answers":["By eating less meat.","Eat less meat.","I can reduce it by eating less meat."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l01-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l01","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Il riscaldamento globale sta cambiando il clima."},"answer":"Global warming is changing the weather.","accepted_answers":["Global warming is changing the climate.","Global warming's changing the weather."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-global-warming"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"drought","right":"siccità"},{"left":"flood","right":"alluvione / inondazione"},{"left":"shortage","right":"scarsità / carenza"},{"left":"threat","right":"minaccia"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-drought","eit-flood","eit-shortage","eit-threat"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":2,"type":"image_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa mostra l’immagine?","payload":{"type":"image_choice","emoji":"🏜️","options":["drought","flood","storm","snow"]},"answer":"drought","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-drought"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"There is a water ___ in three towns.","translation":"C’è carenza d’acqua in tre paesi.","options":["shortage","drought","threat","flood"]},"answer":"shortage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-shortage"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un servizio radiofonico sulla siccità in una regione agricola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Perché i fiumi sono ancora bassi?","options":["Perché i temporali della settimana scorsa non sono bastati dopo otto mesi senza pioggia","Perché gli agricoltori usano troppa acqua","Perché ci sono state alluvioni","Perché hanno chiuso una diga"]},"answer":"Perché i temporali della settimana scorsa non sono bastati dopo otto mesi senza pioggia","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: “This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un servizio radiofonico sulla siccità in una regione agricola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Che cosa c’è di ironico nella situazione, secondo Paula?","options":["Che due anni fa la stessa regione ha subito alluvioni terribili","Che non aveva mai piovuto così tanto","Che gli agricoltori hanno guadagnato di più","Che gli scienziati non conoscono la causa"]},"answer":"Che due anni fa la stessa regione ha subito alluvioni terribili","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: “Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Il riassunto di un rapporto di un’organizzazione ambientalista.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"Chi colpiscono di più le siccità e le alluvioni, secondo il rapporto?","options":["I paesi più poveri, anche se sono quelli che inquinano di meno","I paesi più ricchi","Le grandi aziende","Tutti allo stesso modo"]},"answer":"I paesi più poveri, anche se sono quelli che inquinano di meno","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il rapporto dice: “Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"The flood destroyed many homes.","options":["The flood destroyed many homes.","The flood destroyed many roads.","The storm destroyed many homes.","The floods destroyed a few homes."]},"answer":"The flood destroyed many homes.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-flood"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":8,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (per la siccità)","translation":"Perché in paese non c’è acqua?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-drought"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l02-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l02","position":9,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"È la peggiore siccità degli ultimi cinquant’anni."},"answer":"It is the worst drought in fifty years.","accepted_answers":["It's the worst drought in fifty years.","This is the worst drought in fifty years.","It is the worst drought in 50 years."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-drought"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"carbon footprint","right":"impronta di carbonio"},{"left":"emissions","right":"emissioni"},{"left":"flood","right":"alluvione / inondazione"},{"left":"global warming","right":"riscaldamento globale"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-carbon-footprint","eit-emissions","eit-flood","eit-global-warming"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":2,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why is there no water in the town? (per la siccità)","translation":"Perché in paese non c’è acqua?"},"answer":"Because of the drought.","accepted_answers":["Because there is a drought.","It's because of the drought.","Because of the drought, there is no water."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-drought"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Extreme weather is a ___ of global warming.","translation":"Il clima estremo è una conseguenza del riscaldamento globale.","options":["consequence","emissions","footprint","solution"]},"answer":"consequence","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-consequence"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":4,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["Cars","produce","a","lot","of","emissions"],"translation":"Le auto producono molte emissioni."},"answer":"Cars produce a lot of emissions.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-emissions"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":5,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"alluvione / inondazione"},"answer":"flood","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-flood"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":6,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Scrivi la parola completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"c_r_o_ f_o_p_i_t","hint":"impronta di carbonio"},"answer":"carbon footprint","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["eit-carbon-footprint"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"emissions","options":["emissions","drought","whereas","carbon footprint"]},"answer":"emissions","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-emissions"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":8,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “global warming”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"global warming","options":["riscaldamento globale","anche se / sebbene","in via d’estinzione","conseguenza"]},"answer":"riscaldamento globale","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-global-warming"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":9,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"There is a water ___ in three towns.","translation":"C’è carenza d’acqua in tre paesi.","options":["shortage","drought","threat","flood"]},"answer":"shortage","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-shortage"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev1","position":10,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “drought”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"drought","options":["siccità","anche nel caso in cui / persino se","anche se / sebbene","alluvione / inondazione"]},"answer":"siccità","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-drought"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":1,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ the rain, we went for a walk.","translation":"Nonostante la pioggia, siamo usciti a fare una passeggiata.","options":["Despite","Even though","Although","Even if"]},"answer":"Despite","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Despite + sostantivo (the rain). Even though e although vanno con una frase.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-despite"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ I was tired, I finished the report.","translation":"Anche se ero stanco, ho finito la relazione.","options":["Even though","Despite","In spite of","Whereas"]},"answer":"Even though","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even though + frase completa (I was tired).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-even-though"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In spite ___ the price, I take the train.","translation":"Malgrado il prezzo, prendo il treno.","options":["of","to","for","that"]},"answer":"of","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In spite of (con of); despite va senza of.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-in-spite-of","eit-tackle","eit-sustainable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":4,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ it rains, the game will go ahead.","translation":"Anche se piove, la partita si giocherà.","options":["Even if","Despite","Whereas","In spite of"]},"answer":"Even if","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-even-if"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Due studenti discutono se una persona può aiutare il pianeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Che cosa fa Noah nonostante il prezzo?","options":["Va in treno a trovare la sua famiglia invece di prendere l’aereo","Prende meno l’aereo in vacanza","Va all’università in bici","Ha smesso di mangiare carne"]},"answer":"Va in treno a trovare la sua famiglia invece di prendere l’aereo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Noah dice: “I’ve stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Due studenti discutono se una persona può aiutare il pianeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Che cosa vuol dire Mia con “Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference”?","options":["Che anche se lo facessero tutti, l’effetto sarebbe molto piccolo","Che nessuno smetterà di prendere l’aereo","Che volare non inquina","Che la città è molto piccola"]},"answer":"Che anche se lo facessero tutti, l’effetto sarebbe molto piccolo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Even if: anche nel caso in cui tutti smettessero di volare, il risultato (una differenza minima) non cambierebbe.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-drought","setting":"Un servizio radiofonico sulla siccità in una regione agricola.","speakers":[{"name":"Presenter","voice":"a"},{"name":"Paula","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"We go now to Paula, who is in the south, where there hasn't been any real rain for eight months."},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Thanks. This is the worst drought in fifty years. Despite the storms last week, the rivers are still very low."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"How are farmers dealing with it?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"With great difficulty. Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops. And there is now a water shortage in three towns."},{"speaker":"Presenter","text":"Is this connected to global warming?"},{"speaker":"Paula","text":"Scientists say yes. Ironically, two years ago this same region suffered terrible floods. Extreme weather, in both directions, is a direct consequence of a warmer planet."}]},"question":"Che cosa è successo agli agricoltori anche se hanno ridotto il consumo d’acqua?","options":["Molti hanno perso metà del raccolto","Hanno guadagnato più soldi","Si sono trasferiti in un’altra regione","Non hanno avuto problemi"]},"answer":"Molti hanno perso metà del raccolto","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Paula dice: “Even though they have reduced their water use, many have lost half of their crops”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","options":["Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","Because I was tired, I finished the report.","Even though I was tired, I started the report.","Even though I was busy, I finished the report."]},"answer":"Even though I was tired, I finished the report.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-even-though"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did you go to the beach? (sì, nonostante il freddo)","translation":"Siete andati al mare?"},"answer":"Yes, despite the cold.","accepted_answers":["Yes, in spite of the cold.","Yes, we went despite the cold.","Yes, even though it was cold."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-despite"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l03-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Nonostante la pioggia, siamo usciti a fare una passeggiata."},"answer":"Despite the rain, we went for a walk.","accepted_answers":["In spite of the rain, we went for a walk.","Despite the rain we went for a walk.","We went for a walk despite the rain."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-despite"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"renewable","right":"rinnovabile"},{"left":"sustainable","right":"sostenibile"},{"left":"tackle","right":"affrontare (un problema)"},{"left":"whereas","right":"mentre (invece)"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-renewable","eit-sustainable","eit-tackle","eit-whereas"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I love the city, ___ my brother prefers the country.","translation":"A me piace tantissimo la città, mentre mio fratello preferisce la campagna.","options":["whereas","despite","even if","in spite of"]},"answer":"whereas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Whereas unisce due fatti opposti.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-whereas"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"We need to ___ the real causes of the problem.","translation":"Dobbiamo affrontare le vere cause del problema.","options":["tackle","reduce","produce","protect"]},"answer":"tackle","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Collocazione: tackle a problem (affrontare un problema).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-tackle"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-footprint","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo d’opinione sull’impronta di carbonio.","title":"Your shower will not save the planet","lines":["We are constantly told to reduce our carbon footprint: take shorter showers, eat less meat, fly less. These things matter, but they are not enough.","Just one hundred companies are responsible for most of the world’s emissions. Whereas a single family can save a few tons of CO2 a year, one large factory can produce millions.","This does not mean that individual action is useless. Even if your own impact is small, your choices send a message to companies and governments.","The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy, such as solar and wind. Only governments can make that happen, and only if we vote for it."]},"question":"Qual è la vera soluzione, secondo l’autore?","options":["Passare in fretta all’energia rinnovabile, cosa che possono fare solo i governi","Che ogni famiglia faccia docce brevi","Chiudere tutte le fabbriche","Smettere di votare"]},"answer":"Passare in fretta all’energia rinnovabile, cosa che possono fare solo i governi","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “The real solution is a fast move to renewable energy… Only governments can make that happen”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Due studenti discutono se una persona può aiutare il pianeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Su che cosa finiscono per essere d’accordo Noah e Mia?","options":["Tutti e due vogliono un futuro sostenibile, ma non sono d’accordo su come arrivarci","Tutti e due smetteranno di prendere l’aereo","Non sono d’accordo su niente","Mia accetta che una persona possa cambiare tutto"]},"answer":"Tutti e due vogliono un futuro sostenibile, ma non sono d’accordo su come arrivarci","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mia dice: “So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-students","setting":"Due studenti discutono se una persona può aiutare il pianeta.","speakers":[{"name":"Noah","voice":"a"},{"name":"Mia","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I've stopped flying. In spite of the price, I take the train to visit my family."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"That's great, but honestly, it won't change anything. Even if everyone in this city stopped flying, it would be a tiny difference."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"I don't agree. Big changes always start with small groups of people."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"Maybe. But we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food."},{"speaker":"Noah","text":"Sure, but those things change when people demand something different."},{"speaker":"Mia","text":"OK, that's a fair point. So we both want a sustainable future. We just disagree about how to get there."}]},"question":"Quali cause vuole affrontare Mia?","options":["Il carbone, il petrolio e il modo di produrre il cibo","I voli e i treni","Le docce lunghe","Le grandi città"]},"answer":"Il carbone, il petrolio e il modo di produrre il cibo","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Mia dice: “we need to tackle the real causes: coal, oil, and the way we produce food”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"We need more renewable energy.","options":["We need more renewable energy.","We need less renewable energy.","We need more clean energy.","We have more renewable energy."]},"answer":"We need more renewable energy.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-renewable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["We","all","want","a","sustainable","future"],"translation":"Tutti vogliamo un futuro sostenibile."},"answer":"We all want a sustainable future.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-sustainable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What kind of energy should we use? (energia rinnovabile, come quella solare)","translation":"Che tipo di energia dovremmo usare?"},"answer":"We should use renewable energy, like solar energy.","accepted_answers":["Renewable energy, like solar energy.","We should use renewable energy.","Renewable energy, such as solar."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-renewable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l04-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l04","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Dobbiamo affrontare le vere cause del problema."},"answer":"We need to tackle the real causes of the problem.","accepted_answers":["We have to tackle the real causes of the problem.","We must tackle the real causes of the problem."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-tackle"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":1,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What kind of energy should we use? (energia rinnovabile, come quella solare)","translation":"Che tipo di energia dovremmo usare?"},"answer":"We should use renewable energy, like solar energy.","accepted_answers":["Renewable energy, like solar energy.","We should use renewable energy.","Renewable energy, such as solar."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-renewable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"grammar","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"___ the rain, we went for a walk.","translation":"Nonostante la pioggia, siamo usciti a fare una passeggiata.","options":["Despite","Even though","Although","Even if"]},"answer":"Despite","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Despite + sostantivo (the rain). Even though e although vanno con una frase.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-despite"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":3,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"renewable","options":["renewable","in spite of","drought","sustainable"]},"answer":"renewable","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-renewable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":4,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “even though”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"even though","options":["anche se / sebbene","alluvione / inondazione","in via d’estinzione","riscaldamento globale"]},"answer":"anche se / sebbene","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-even-though"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":5,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “in spite of”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"in spite of","options":["malgrado / a dispetto di","anche nel caso in cui / persino se","scarsità / carenza","alluvione / inondazione"]},"answer":"malgrado / a dispetto di","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-in-spite-of"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":6,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"In spite ___ the price, I take the train.","translation":"Malgrado il prezzo, prendo il treno.","options":["of","to","for","that"]},"answer":"of","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"In spite of (con of); despite va senza of.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-in-spite-of","eit-tackle","eit-sustainable"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":7,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Dobbiamo affrontare le vere cause del problema."},"answer":"We need to tackle the real causes of the problem.","accepted_answers":["We have to tackle the real causes of the problem.","We must tackle the real causes of the problem."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-tackle"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":8,"type":"complete_word","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Scrivi la parola completa","payload":{"type":"complete_word","masked":"w_e_e_s","hint":"mentre (invece)"},"answer":"whereas","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":20,"words":["eit-whereas"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":9,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “tackle”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"tackle","options":["affrontare (un problema)","povertà","malgrado / a dispetto di","rinnovabile"]},"answer":"affrontare (un problema)","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-tackle"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-rev2","position":10,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"even though","right":"anche se / sebbene"},{"left":"renewable","right":"rinnovabile"},{"left":"tackle","right":"affrontare (un problema)"},{"left":"whereas","right":"mentre (invece)"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-even-though","eit-renewable","eit-tackle","eit-whereas"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":1,"type":"translation_choice","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Che cosa significa “poverty”?","payload":{"type":"translation_choice","word":"poverty","options":["povertà","minaccia","scarsità / carenza","siccità"]},"answer":"povertà","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":12,"words":["eit-poverty"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The panda is an ___ animal.","translation":"Il panda è un animale in via d’estinzione.","options":["endangered","renewable","sustainable","dangerous"]},"answer":"endangered","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Endangered: in pericolo (minacciato). Dangerous: pericoloso (che causa pericolo).","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-endangered"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"Climate change is a ___ to people and nature.","translation":"Il cambiamento climatico è una minaccia per le persone e la natura.","options":["threat","shortage","drought","poverty"]},"answer":"threat","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-threat"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Il riassunto di un rapporto di un’organizzazione ambientalista.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"Perché ci sono così tante specie in pericolo, secondo il rapporto?","options":["Soprattutto per la perdita delle foreste e l’inquinamento degli oceani","Per la caccia","Solo per le siccità","Per il turismo"]},"answer":"Soprattutto per la perdita delle foreste e l’inquinamento degli oceani","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il rapporto dice: “More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Il riassunto di un rapporto di un’organizzazione ambientalista.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"Come sono collegati la povertà e l’ambiente, secondo il rapporto?","options":["Le persone povere a volte non hanno altra scelta che tagliare le foreste per sopravvivere","Non hanno nessun legame","I paesi poveri inquinano di più","La povertà protegge le foreste"]},"answer":"Le persone povere a volte non hanno altra scelta che tagliare le foreste per sopravvivere","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il rapporto dice: “when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u7-report","document":"notice","setting":"Il riassunto di un rapporto di un’organizzazione ambientalista.","title":"Our planet: 2026 report","lines":["Key findings of our annual report:","More than one million species are endangered, mainly because of the loss of forests and the pollution of oceans.","Climate change is a growing threat not only to nature, but to people. Floods and droughts hit the poorest countries hardest, even though they produce the lowest emissions.","Poverty and the environment are connected: when people are poor, they often have no choice but to cut down forests to survive.","Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years, which shows that action works."]},"question":"Qual è la buona notizia del rapporto?","options":["Diverse specie sono state salvate, il che dimostra che agire funziona","Non ci sono più specie in pericolo","Le emissioni sono diminuite","La siccità è finita"]},"answer":"Diverse specie sono state salvate, il che dimostra che agire funziona","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Il rapporto dice: “Despite these problems, there is good news. Several species have been saved in the last ten years”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"Poverty and the environment are connected.","options":["Poverty and the environment are connected.","Poverty and the environment are not connected.","Poverty and pollution are connected.","Poverty and the climate are connected."]},"answer":"Poverty and the environment are connected.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-poverty"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["The","panda","is","an","endangered","animal"],"translation":"Il panda è un animale in via d’estinzione."},"answer":"The panda is an endangered animal.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-endangered"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"What is the biggest global problem, in your opinion? (la povertà)","translation":"Secondo te, qual è il problema globale più grande?"},"answer":"In my opinion, it is poverty.","accepted_answers":["In my opinion, it's poverty.","Poverty.","I think it is poverty."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-poverty"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u07-l05-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u07-l05","position":10,"typ