options":["to answer","answering","answer","of answering"]},"answer":"to answer","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Refuse to + verbo.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-refuse"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Un’intervista televisiva a un politico.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"Di che cosa ha accusato un giornale il partito di Hart?","options":["Di usare denaro pubblico per la sua campagna","Di mentire in un’intervista","Di chiudere uffici del governo","Di non pagare le tasse"]},"answer":"Di usare denaro pubblico per la sua campagna","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"La giornalista dice: “a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Un’intervista televisiva a un politico.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"Che cosa ha ammesso Hart la settimana prima, secondo lui?","options":["Di aver usato un ufficio per una riunione","Di aver usato denaro pubblico","Di aver mentito","Niente"]},"answer":"Di aver usato un ufficio per una riunione","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hart dice: “I admitted using one office for one meeting. That’s very different”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":7,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u8-interview","setting":"Un’intervista televisiva a un politico.","speakers":[{"name":"Journalist","voice":"a"},{"name":"Hart","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Mr. Hart, a newspaper has accused your party of using public money for its campaign. Is that true?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I completely deny that. Every dollar we spent was ours."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"But you admitted last week that the campaign had used government offices."},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I admitted using one office for one meeting. That's very different."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Will you publish the campaign accounts?"},{"speaker":"Hart","text":"I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven't done anything wrong."},{"speaker":"Journalist","text":"Many viewers will find that answer hard to believe."}]},"question":"Che cosa fa Hart quando gli chiedono dei conti della campagna?","options":["Si rifiuta di rispondere e dice che sono voci","Promette di pubblicarli","Ammette che ci sono stati errori","Dà la colpa alla giornalista"]},"answer":"Si rifiuta di rispondere e dice che sono voci","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hart dice: “I refuse to answer questions based on rumors. I insist that we haven’t done anything wrong”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":8,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"She admitted making a mistake.","options":["She admitted making a mistake.","She denied making a mistake.","She admitted making a promise.","He admitted making a mistake."]},"answer":"She admitted making a mistake.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-admit"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Did he say he took the money? (no, ha negato di averli presi)","translation":"Ha detto di aver preso i soldi?"},"answer":"No, he denied taking it.","accepted_answers":["No, he denied taking the money.","He denied taking it.","No. He denied taking it."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-deny"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l03-e10","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l03","position":10,"type":"translate_write","skill":"translation","prompt_es":"Traduci in inglese","payload":{"type":"translate_write","source":"Lo hanno accusato di mentire."},"answer":"They accused him of lying.","accepted_answers":["He was accused of lying.","They accused him of telling lies."],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-accuse"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l04-e01","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l04","position":1,"type":"match_pairs","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Abbina ogni parola al suo significato","payload":{"type":"match_pairs","pairs":[{"left":"reliable","right":"affidabile / attendibile"},{"left":"biased","right":"di parte / fazioso"},{"left":"misleading","right":"fuorviante / ingannevole"},{"left":"fact-check","right":"verificare (i fatti)"}]},"answer":"","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":30,"words":["eit-reliable","eit-biased","eit-misleading","eit-fact-check"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l04-e02","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l04","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"The article is ___. It only shows one side.","translation":"L’articolo è di parte. Mostra solo un lato.","options":["biased","reliable","viral","official"]},"answer":"biased","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-biased"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l04-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l04","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"That headline is ___. The article says nothing new.","translation":"Quel titolo è un acchiappaclic. L’articolo non dice niente di nuovo.","options":["clickbait","reliable","misinformation","rumor"]},"answer":"clickbait","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-clickbait"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l04-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l04","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u8-guide","document":"post","setting":"Una guida per riconoscere le informazioni false.","title":"Think before you share","lines":["Five questions to ask before you share a story","1. Who wrote it? Reliable sources tell you who the journalist is and where the information comes from.","2. Does the headline match the story? Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different.","3. Is it one-sided? A biased article only shows one side and ignores facts that do not support its argument.","4. Are the numbers misleading? A \"300% rise\" sounds huge, but it may mean the number went from one to four.","5. Have other media reported it? If nobody else has the story, be careful. Check it on a fact-checking site."]},"question":"Secondo la guida, che cosa fanno i titoli clickbait?","options":["Promettono qualcosa di scioccante per farti cliccare, ma l’articolo dice un’altra cosa","Riassumono bene l’articolo","Danno il nome del giornalista","Mostrano i due lati"]},"answer":"Promettono qualcosa di scioccante per farti cliccare, ma l’articolo dice un’altra cosa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"La guida dice: “Clickbait headlines promise something shocking to make you click, but the article often says something different”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u08-l04-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u08-l04","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u8-guide","document":"post","setting":"Una guida per riconoscere le informazioni false.","title":"Think before you share","lines":["Five questions to ask before you share a story","1. Who wrote it? Reliable sources tell you who the journalist is and where the information comes from.","2. 