t-b2-u10-l02-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Alcuni colleghi discutono la proposta di lavorare quattro giorni a settimana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Che cosa preoccupa Olivia della settimana di quattro giorni?","options":["Chi seguirà i clienti il venerdì","Guadagnare meno","Lavorare più ore","Che Ken non ci sia"]},"answer":"Chi seguirà i clienti il venerdì","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Olivia dice: “What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u10-l02-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u10-four-days","setting":"Alcuni colleghi discutono la proposta di lavorare quattro giorni a settimana.","speakers":[{"name":"Olivia","voice":"a"},{"name":"Ken","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"So, the four-day week. What worries me is the customers. Who answers the phone on Fridays?"},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"We'd take turns. The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they're rested."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"That may be true for some jobs. But we need to take into account that our clients expect us every day."},{"speaker":"Ken","text":"That's a valid point. So let's try it for three months and measure the results."},{"speaker":"Olivia","text":"OK, I find that convincing. All things considered, a trial is a good compromise."}]},"question":"Secondo Ken, perché altre aziende hanno adottato la settimana di quattro giorni?","options":["Perché la gente lavora meglio quando è riposata","Perché risparmiano soldi","Perché l’hanno chiesto i clienti","Perché è la legge"]},"answer":"Perché la gente lavora meglio quando è riposata","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Ken dice: “The reason why other companies have done it is that people work better when they’re rested”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u10-l02-e06","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":6,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u10-school-debate","setting":"Un dibattito a scuola: bisogna vietare i telefoni in classe?","speakers":[{"name":"Moderator","voice":"a"},{"name":"Lucas","voice":"b"},{"name":"Hannah","voice":"a"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Today's debate: should phones be banned in schools? Lucas, you're first."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"Yes, they should. Phones distract students. Moreover, they make bullying easier, because it continues after school. As a result, many students feel anxious all day."},{"speaker":"Moderator","text":"Hannah, your answer?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly."},{"speaker":"Lucas","text":"But that's an assumption. Where is the evidence that teaching works better?"},{"speaker":"Hannah","text":"Fair question. What I'm saying is that a ban doesn't teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home."}]},"question":"Che cosa chiarisce Hannah con “In other words…”?","options":["Che con il divieto gli studenti useranno solo di più il telefono a casa","Che i telefoni sono pericolosi","Che è d’accordo con Lucas","Che non ha prove"]},"answer":"Che con il divieto gli studenti useranno solo di più il telefono a casa","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dice: “a ban doesn’t teach anything. In other words, students will just use their phones more at home”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u10-l02-e07","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":7,"type":"listen_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e scegli quello che senti","payload":{"type":"listen_choice","audioText":"What matters is that you tried.","options":["What matters is that you tried.","What matters is that you won.","It doesn't matter that you tried.","What matters is that we tried."]},"answer":"What matters is that you tried.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u10-l02-e08","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":8,"type":"order_words","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Metti le parole in ordine","payload":{"type":"order_words","tokens":["What","worries","me","is","the","cost"],"translation":"Quello che mi preoccupa è il costo."},"answer":"What worries me is the cost.","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":25,"words":["eit-what-matters-is"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u10-l02-e09","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u10-l02","position":9,"type":"short_answer","skill":"sentence_building","prompt_es":"Rispondi in inglese","payload":{"type":"short_answer","question":"Why are you studying English? (il motivo è che vuoi lavorare all’ester