n_id":"eit-b2-u12-l01","position":2,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"I am weighing ___ the pros and cons.","translation":"Sto soppesando i pro e i contro.","options":["up","out","down","off"]},"answer":"up","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-weigh-up"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u12-l01-e03","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u12-l01","position":3,"type":"fill_blank","skill":"vocabulary","prompt_es":"Completa la frase","payload":{"type":"fill_blank","sentence":"More money, less free time: that is the ___.","translation":"Più soldi, meno tempo libero: questo è il prezzo da pagare.","options":["trade-off","dilemma","problem","decision"]},"answer":"trade-off","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":null,"difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":15,"words":["eit-trade-off"]},{"id":"eit-b2-u12-l01-e04","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u12-l01","position":4,"type":"context_choice","skill":"listening","prompt_es":"Ascolta e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"listening","id":"eit.stim.b2-u12-job-offer","setting":"Un’amica racconta a un’altra che deve decidere se trasferirsi per lavoro.","speakers":[{"name":"Alice","voice":"a"},{"name":"Rosa","voice":"b"}],"rate":1,"lines":[{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I've got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"That's amazing! So why do you look worried?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"Because I'd have to move in a month. I've been weighing up the pros and cons all week."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"What does your gut feeling say?"},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"To go. But I'm having second thoughts because of my parents. They're getting older."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Remember two years ago, when you turned down the job in Berlin? If you had taken it, you'd be speaking German by now."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"Qual è il dilemma di Alice?","options":["Se accettare un posto a Lisbona e trasferirsi entro un mese","Se cambiare carriera","Se trasferirsi a Berlino","Se lasciare il lavoro per occuparsi dei genitori"]},"answer":"Se accettare un posto a Lisbona e trasferirsi entro un mese","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dice: “I’ve got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager… I’d have to move in a month”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"words":[]},{"id":"eit-b2-u12-l01-e05","lesson_id":"eit-b2-u12-l01","position":5,"type":"context_choice","skill":"reading","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo su come prendere decisioni importanti.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"Secondo l’articolo, perché le grandi decisioni sono difficili?","options":["Perché si guadagna sempre qualcosa in cambio di perdere qualcos’altro","Perché non ci sono mai informazioni","Perché la gente è insicura","Perché richiedono molto tempo"]},"answer":"Perché si guadagna sempre qualcosa in cambio di perdere qualcos’altro","accepted_answers":[],"exp