 ma propone di insegnare a usarli bene","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Hannah dice: “Admittedly, phones can be a distraction. Nevertheless, banning them is not the answer. On the contrary, schools should teach students how to use them responsibly”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"eit.ex.4calv6k8szylsj","content_hash":"v1:110ea6845121cc4c072a28bfd3b1e2787e45c893500a9f7c2e030b1fe1e21e11","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u10-free-uni","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo d’opinione sull’università gratuita.","title":"Education is an investment, not a cost","lines":["Should university be free? I believe it should.","First, education benefits everyone, not only the student. Educated citizens earn more, pay more taxes and are healthier. Furthermore, free education gives poor students the same chances as rich ones.","Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money, and some people argue that students should pay for their own future. Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs.","It is not the cost of education that should worry us, but the cost of ignorance.","To sum up, free university is not a gift. It is an investment in all of us."]},"question":"Che cosa riconosce l’autrice e come lo ribatte?","options":["Che costa molto allo Stato, ma i benefici a lungo termine sono maggiori","Che è ingiusto, ma necessario","Che gli studenti non lo apprezzano","Che è impossibile, ma bisogna provarci"]},"answer":"Che costa molto allo Stato, ma i benefici a lungo termine sono maggiori","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"L’articolo dice: “Admittedly, free universities cost the government a lot of money… Nevertheless, the long-term benefits outweigh the costs”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":60,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_v