ow."},{"speaker":"Alice","text":"I know. And if I were braver, I would have said yes immediately this time too."},{"speaker":"Rosa","text":"Every choice has a trade-off. But Lisbon is only a short flight away. You could visit them often."}]},"question":"Qual è il dilemma di Alice?","options":["Se accettare un posto a Lisbona e trasferirsi entro un mese","Se cambiare carriera","Se trasferirsi a Berlino","Se lasciare il lavoro per occuparsi dei genitori"]},"answer":"Se accettare un posto a Lisbona e trasferirsi entro un mese","accepted_answers":[],"explanation_es":"Alice dice: “I’ve got a real dilemma. The Lisbon office has offered me a job as team manager… I’d have to move in a month”.","difficulty":1,"recommended_seconds":75,"grading_spec":{"mode":"exact_option","mode_version":1},"generator":null,"generator_version":null},{"item_id":"eit.ex.79tejoib1m2p7r","content_hash":"v1:ec04656d14f4efa252f57a5815de8c717c96bfea8d9a541c457bf1a1644226fc","prompt_es":"Leggi e rispondi","payload":{"type":"context_choice","stimulus":{"kind":"reading","id":"eit.stim.b2-u12-guide","document":"post","setting":"Un articolo su come prendere decisioni importanti.","title":"How to make a big decision","lines":["Big decisions are hard because there is always a trade-off: more money but less free time, adventure but less security.","First, write down the pros and cons. Seeing them on paper helps you weigh them up more calmly.","Second, ask yourself what is really at stake. Will this matter in five years? If not, do not spend weeks on it.","Third, listen to your gut feeling. Research suggests that our first reaction often contains information we are not aware of.","Finally, accept that no decision is perfect. If we had a crystal ball, we would never make mistakes. We do not, so we learn from them."]},"question":"Secondo l’articolo, perché le grandi decisioni sono difficili?","options":["Perché si guadagna sempre qualcosa in cambio di perdere qualcos’altro","Perché non ci sono mai informazioni"